  "label": "Starvation Stereotype",
  "description": "The text 'starving mexican' invokes the stereotype that Mexicans are chronically poor and hungry, implying they are unable to afford basic necessities. This is a false and harmful stereotype that perpetuates economic racism and ignores the economic diversity and achievements of the Mexican population. It is often used to justify immigration restrictions or to portray Mexicans as a burden on society.",
